commit 735ddf815aba38f5a822d406bc309040c1683306
Author: Christie Hubley <christie@tinkerartstudio.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 27 23:14:26 2026 -0600

    fix: copied-camp review — implementation review round 2 (Codex + Claude)
    
    Both: an auto-save that SKIPS (empty camp name, or a concurrent-save early return) wrote nothing but
    left the failure flag clear, so Mark reviewed could still succeed with the grid change unsaved.
    
    - curriculumAutoSaveUnsavedId replaces the global failure flag: set by the auto-save that failed OR
      skipped, keyed by camp doc id (another camp is never blocked — r2 LOW), cleared by that camp's next
      successful auto-save and on opening the editor (the form is refilled from the stored camp)
    - autoSaveCurriculum writes to the id it captured at its start
    - Mark/Undo and each editor opening take an operation number; only the latest clears the in-flight
      lock, so camp A's finishing write can't re-enable camp B's button mid-write
    - the flush gives up after 20 s (offline writes never settle) and says so, instead of holding the
      editor open for good; refused close / Cancel now say "Finishing the last save — one moment."
    - tests: empty-name skip blocks the review (red on the previous commit); the "cannot be switched"
      test now really tries to open another camp
    
    e2e 144/144.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

